# Caddy in front of the Gryphon agent: TLS from Let's Encrypt, and the agent
# itself on loopback. Replace the name with the host's own; its DNS must point
# here and ports 80 and 443 must be open for the certificate.
#
# Caddy passes the Authorization header through as it is, which the agent
# needs. Do not add authentication of Caddy's own: Gryphon sends only the
# agent's key.
agent.example.com {
	reverse_proxy 127.0.0.1:6001
}
